Fetch the toolchain's zlib runtime from an immutable mirror.

rules_rs vendors a `libz.so.1` into the rustc repository, because upstream's
Linux rustc bundles a libLLVM that links against it dynamically. It takes that
library out of an Ubuntu `.deb` pinned by URL and sha256 in
`rs/private/rustc_repository.bzl`.

The URLs it pins point into the live `archive.ubuntu.com` and
`ports.ubuntu.com` pools, which only ever hold a package's *current* build.
Ubuntu superseded `zlib1g 1:1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.1` with `3.1ubuntu2.2` and
deleted the old file, so both pinned URLs now return 404 and every Bazel
invocation that has to fetch `@rules_rs++toolchains+rustc_linux_*` fails during
analysis, before a single crate compiles. Warm repository caches hid it for a
few hours; cold ones do not.

Repointing at `3.1ubuntu2.2` would only reset the clock -- zlib is in `main`
and gets an SRU or security respin every few months, each of which deletes its
predecessor. The two mirrors below are immutable by construction instead:

  * `snapshot.ubuntu.com` serves the archive as it stood at a timestamp, and
    Canonical publishes it precisely so that a pinned build stays fetchable
    after the pool moves on. A given timestamp's contents never change.
  * `launchpadlibrarian.net` addresses a file by the id Launchpad assigned when
    the build was published. Ids are never reused and files are never removed,
    so the URL outlives the publication itself.

Passing both as a list makes Bazel try them in turn, so the fetch also survives
one of the two services being down. Neither can be invalidated by the next
respin, which is the failure this patch exists to stop recurring.

The pinned version and sha256s are unchanged -- this moves where the bytes come
from, not which bytes. Both mirrors were verified to serve the exact sha256s
already in the file, for both architectures.

Upstream carries no fix: 0.0.107 is the newest release in the BCR, and its
`rustc_repository.bzl` is byte-identical to the one on `main`.

--- a/rs/private/rustc_repository.bzl
+++ b/rs/private/rustc_repository.bzl
@@ -51,23 +51,34 @@
 )
 """
 
+# The live `archive.ubuntu.com` and `ports.ubuntu.com` pools hold only the
+# current build of a package: a security or SRU respin deletes its predecessor,
+# and every pinned pool URL 404s from that moment on. Both mirrors below are
+# immutable instead -- a snapshot timestamp and a librarian file id each name
+# one byte sequence forever -- so the next respin cannot break this fetch.
 _LINUX_ZLIB = {
     "aarch64": struct(
         libdir = "usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu",
         sha256 = "cbe3d39ec32d3cc27c021ae4af11e7c67bdf9d700d573207e0941d4038056278",
-        url = "https://ports.ubuntu.com/ubuntu-ports/pool/main/z/zlib/zlib1g_1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.1_arm64.deb",
+        urls = [
+            "https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/20250601T000000Z/pool/main/z/zlib/zlib1g_1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.1_arm64.deb",
+            "https://launchpadlibrarian.net/742994699/zlib1g_1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.1_arm64.deb",
+        ],
     ),
     "x86_64": struct(
         libdir = "usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu",
         sha256 = "7074b6a2f6367a10d280c00a1cb02e74277709180bab4f2491a2f355ab2d6c20",
-        url = "https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/z/zlib/zlib1g_1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.1_amd64.deb",
+        urls = [
+            "https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/20250601T000000Z/pool/main/z/zlib/zlib1g_1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.1_amd64.deb",
+            "https://launchpadlibrarian.net/742985810/zlib1g_1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.1_amd64.deb",
+        ],
     ),
 }
 
-def _extract_deb_payload(rctx, url, sha256, output, strip_prefix):
+def _extract_deb_payload(rctx, urls, sha256, output, strip_prefix):
     deb_dir = ".zlib_deb"
     rctx.download_and_extract(
-        url = url,
+        url = urls,
         sha256 = sha256,
         output = deb_dir,
         type = ".deb",
@@ -75,7 +86,7 @@
 
     data_archive = deb_dir + "/data.tar.zst"
     if not rctx.path(data_archive).exists:
-        fail("expected data.tar.zst in {}".format(url))
+        fail("expected data.tar.zst in {}".format(", ".join(urls)))
 
     rctx.extract(data_archive, output = output, stripPrefix = strip_prefix)
     rctx.delete(deb_dir)
@@ -85,7 +96,7 @@
         return
 
     zlib = _LINUX_ZLIB[exec_triple.arch]
-    _extract_deb_payload(rctx, zlib.url, zlib.sha256, "lib", zlib.libdir)
+    _extract_deb_payload(rctx, zlib.urls, zlib.sha256, "lib", zlib.libdir)
 
 def _symlink_rust_objcopy_shared_libraries(rctx, exec_triple):
     top_level_lib = rctx.path("lib")
